:[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Climate Transition, Corporate and Environmental Services Policy Advisory Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Planning and Healthier Stronger Communities Policy Advisory Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Housing and Community Cohesion Policy Advisory Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Climate Transition, Corporate and Environmental Services Policy Advisory Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Planning and Healthier Stronger Communities Policy Advisory Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Housing and Community Cohesion Policy Advisory Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://services.maidstone.gov.uk/meetings"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Maidstone accounts pass audit as housing rents controls flagged","lead":"Maidstone Council's accounts for 2025/26 passed external audit with no material concerns about the council's ability to continue operating, and arrangements for managing its money deemed adequate. But internal audit identified significant weaknesses in controls over housing rents operations, with 37 findings (3 high-severity) affecting how the council sets rents, collects income, records transactions and manages empty properties and bad debts. These control gaps expose the service to potential lost income and fraud. The external auditor recommended establishing a long-term savings programme, but the council plans instead to rely on annual reviews of its medium-term financial strategy, the council's five-year spending plan. General Fund reserves (money set aside as a financial cushion) stood at \u00a317 million at the start of the year, with a \u00a34 million minimum floor.","iso":"2026-09-28","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Audit Findings Report 2025/26","paper_url":"https://maidstone.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s106548/106548.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Enc. 1 for Audit Governance and Standards Committee Annual Report 2025/26","paper_url":"https://maidstone.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s106529/106529.pdf","headline":"The committee appointed an independent member to strengthen governance capacity.","detail":"The committee added an independent member with relevant skills and experience to support delivery of its audit and governance functions. The chairman identified this appointment as a key highlight of the year, indicating the council views it as a material governance strengthening.","category":"governance","matters":"Independent expert membership strengthens audit committee scrutiny and judgment; this shows the council is actively developing governance capacity.","figures":"1 independent member appointed","quote":"the committee has also appointed an independent member with relevant skills and experience to support the committee in the delivery of its functions","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Enc. 1 for Audit Governance and Standards Committee Annual Report 2025/26","paper_url":"https://maidstone.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s106529/106529.pdf","headline":"The committee structure combines audit and standards functions, departing from CIPFA best practice by deliberate choice.","detail":"CIPFA best practice recommends audit committees operate standalone, but Maidstone has deliberately chosen to combine audit and standards functions. The committee acknowledges this is non-compliant with best practice but states this choice will not be reviewed. CIPFA guidance accepts such structures are sometimes necessary in smaller authorities.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender might view combined governance structures as reducing audit committee independence; a finance director should be aware the council is knowingly accepting a less-than-best-practice model.","figures":"None","quote":"There was one area of non-compliance on the subject of the committee being combined with other functions. It is considered best practice for Audit Committees to be standalone, however, in smaller local authorities it is noted that it is not always possible to have standalone committees for every function due to the total number of members within the Council. Maidstone Borough Council has made the decision to combine the Standards Committee function with the Audit Committee function and this will not be subject to review.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Enc. 1 for Audit Governance and Standards Committee Annual Report 2025/26","paper_url":"https://maidstone.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s106529/106529.pdf","headline":"Internal audit delivered a positive opinion on the council's governance, risk management and control arrangements.","detail":"The Head of Internal Audit Partnership provided a positive annual opinion for 2024/25, covering the overall adequacy and effectiveness of the council's governance, risk management and control framework. This provides independent assurance that control arrangements and governance are sound.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender assessing creditworthiness needs independent confirmation that the council has adequate governance and controls in place; a finance director needs external assurance that their control environment is effective.","figures":"None","quote":"The Council received a positive Annual Opinion from the Head of Internal Audit. This opinion considers the overall adequacy and effectiveness of the authority's framework of governance, risk management and control arrangements.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2_Statement of Accounts 2025-26 for AGS 280926","paper_url":"https://maidstone.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s106552/106552.pdf","headline":"Council's operating activities consumed \u00a314.3m cash in 2025/26; funded by drawing down investments by \u00a326.7m","detail":"The Council's operating activities generated negative cash flow of \u00a314.324m, meaning day-to-day services required cash outflows beyond income received. To maintain a positive cash balance, the Council drew down short-term investments from \u00a320m to \u00a310m. This shows core operations are not self-sufficient and depend on asset sales to cover cash shortfalls.","category":"other","matters":"Cash generation is the ultimate test of financial health. Negative operating cash flows signal structural operating deficits that erode reserves over time and indicate diminishing capacity to service debt.","figures":"Operating activities: negative \u00a314,324k. Investing activities: positive \u00a326,729k (investments drawn down). Short-term investments: fell from \u00a320,000k to \u00a310,000k.","quote":"Net cash flows from Operating activities (14,324) Investing Activities 26,729","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit, Governance and Standards Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2_Statement of Accounts 2025-26 for AGS 280926","paper_url":"https://maidstone.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s106552/106552.pdf","headline":"Government White Paper indicates district councils will likely cease to exist by April 2028; council has taken no account of implications","detail":"The Council's accounting judgements note states that the Government's December 2024 devolution White Paper indicates 'it is likely that district councils will not exist after April 2028.' The Council explicitly records that 'No account has been taken of any potential implications in this report.' This creates material structural uncertainty about the council's existence, functions, asset disposition, and borrowing liability within three years.","category":"governance","matters":"For a lender considering medium or long-term lending to a local authority, potential abolition within the forecast horizon represents fundamental structural risk. It raises unquantified questions about liability transfer, asset custody, and borrowing succession that have not been assessed.","figures":"Government reform timeline: April 2028 (3 years from 18 September 2026)","quote":"It is likely that district councils will not exist after April 2028. The White Paper will have implications over the lifetime of the medium term but does not immediately impact the financial accounts. No account has been taken of any potential implications in this report.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-27"},"name":"Maidstone","findings_total":149,"news_drafts_total":1}}